{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_201","t":"","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#201","p":9,"im":["fe48c480d9ad44c4c975748a4ff359438889b928"],"m":201},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_202","t":"Hi If\n\nThank you very much for your patience. I hope I got it this time. Communication problem from my side. Sorry\n\nRe-submit of example 4. In this example, in reality there have been 2 attempts of compression toward supply (orange triangles) before all demand has been consumed.\n\nCheers\n\nR.","a":"Rogeid16","d":"","n":"#202","p":9,"im":["690ae479956d505c486722ca7e6ff132a5790953"],"m":202},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_203","t":"Ifmyante\n\nChief Cook and Bottle Washer\n\nIf you see a piece of truth glistening in the dirt, get down on your knees and gently dig it out, for it's the greatest treasure you\n\nwill ever find\n\nAlmost","a":"—","d":"","n":"#203","p":9,"im":["b1514e80b374a9af50420c313c576726a3c4c988"],"m":203},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_204","t":"You 'll be a Saint one day. LOL Tx again R.","a":"Rogeid16","d":"","n":"#204","p":9,"im":[],"m":204},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_205","t":"Hello!\n\nThis is part of my homework for Compression part, please check it and feel free to give opinions.\n\nThanks,Saso\n\nCHART 1:\n\nCHART 2:\n\nCHART 3:\n\nCHART 4:\n\nCHART 5:\n\nCHART 6:\n\nCHART 7:","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#205","p":9,"im":["63f505db67f777b4d05db0ea7bba8f12960f9899","0fd4f6af95155c187a33a728f7dffeff5d877db8","3d196441eb4c9478784f9d1f19675c61e00e4dc1","0d2c3a8e08231509bff08778c7aff7c1e629e2da","7f671a9f81ec4c46fa86808bcc2c47b6f5efad2d","51c1d55cbd8954e036cb33ba87d2829fe66760fc","b94e01bcd91dba52441c2273dbcc25d3f35d1c50"],"m":205},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_206","t":"AU","a":"justinforex","d":"","n":"#206","p":9,"im":["7e23c37910d76412b8972804ad9fc2be783e7519"],"m":206},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_207","t":"Hi everyone,\n\nMy first Compression + Liquidity Spike homework.\n\nI based the study on the most recent EU price action.\n\nHope it's on the right track.","a":"Simon","d":"","n":"#207","p":9,"im":["7673276c2c222d52d901315ffdded9128d46ef8e","7b34c2b7c7dd8d0e8e3983b44424cfd8b310d68d"],"m":207},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_208","t":"Some examples of what I think are compression on the kiwi and ozzie along with a couple of other observations which may or may not be important. Any comments / advice would be gratefully received.\n\nThanks\n\nBarfly","a":"barfly","d":"","n":"#208","p":9,"im":["96e8af2974799a495976c7990bd66a7820c66b85","c8a91302921100c9667ff6dcacad3df4a55792b8"],"m":208},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_209","t":"Hello everyone. I lurked on PIE for a while and responded a bit but due to being young and having 2 children my time and capital contributions have been slim. I think everything you guys do is fantastic and I hope my 3 years will give me both the ability to contribute and help others,as well as be the foundation for my own growth.\n\nIdentifying compression and justifying the use of it has been something I have had trouble with. This homework will be the best start!","a":"HoyPip12","d":"","n":"#209","p":9,"im":["e5dcba57fe5f864d05658e08db3c1db04ee8a54b"],"m":209},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_210","t":"You're on the right track with this homework. Just remember to be aware of untested zones as you progress.\n\nBest\n\nIf","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#210","p":9,"im":[],"m":210},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_211","t":"what will help you to start with is marking S/D areas, SR’s or simly decision points and see if price returned to take them out. Compression Definition by Ifmyante. “We talk about compression when price taking out last decision point and the orders that where left there\".","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#211","p":9,"im":[],"m":211},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_212","t":"CHART 8:\n\nCHART 9:\n\nCHART 10:\n\nCHART 11:\n\nCHART 12:\n\nCHART 13:\n\nCHART 14:\n\nCHART 15:","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#212","p":9,"im":["4fb37c36f26d3a29a32221b89b247543c88241aa","7144f578317da83eb28e68b16ce86b61a2f034d9","039786626b7512b484b4cfa35eb3e5b6aea58f22","a970b53a46d7f7660e16c19968597feac49c773b","cbb0189bec16a2d06d4e88577d6c86f589e89740","439e303001eb30c571defbc257031ecaa9024563","1a95355bfd1a23bbef01f1d678e79055b6d5ca03","7bb13b6184924f2a2e5bd1b8d9e7ccacd1704557"],"m":212},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_213","t":"CHART 16:\n\nCHART 17:\n\nCHART 18:\n\nCHART 19:\n\nCHART 20:","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#213","p":9,"im":["10537e439f0008f74db120caeac8cdc7d7f03c99","d487df59f6d5426e2f54e7f37cb45dbd8df0f924","91710ed9459a03099c516e08dcd11dcb663f2392","25f2f3cb291c22791c7ab7b566314643a496159c","ce0790bab2b272ba71ee5a3358863e204d546210"],"m":213},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_214","t":"Im looking at my charts and attempting to find Compression zones into Demand or supply. One thing that worries me is that since im browsing history, i will naturally only look out for compression zones which \"worked out\" and ignore ones which would have failed. Ill try to look for ones which failed and ideally the more experienced traders can point out why those setups failed.\n\nAnyone can point out why this failed?\n\nIll post more soon","a":"nagato","d":"","n":"#214","p":9,"im":["abdd901a6fcfa4695efd994188b5ff22b859c158","1039ed6e8c0bf5a188d4bb4d43b85a715516613d","b5b5b8f328dce5b3ff991e17776783fbb5b35c96","cf08f4f72c37a80da88f9d3567b297edce3d6d16","32541444e04941ea57140707d7776c1fae77b0a4"],"m":214},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_215","t":"Hi Nasgato,\n\nNice that you opened a \"homework thread\". I took a look at your charts and notticed a few things that I would like to point out to you. I have marked a few things on your charts.\n\nAn important point for you would be to not forget about the supply and demand zone first. A broken supply or demand level is also a zone (very important) so before searching for any compression on a chart, maybe it would be beter to look for the the supply and demand zones that are above and bellow current price, then look to see if ther are \"fresh\" or not and only after finding your s/d zones you can look for compression in order to make a decision. If a supply or demand zone has been tested several times, you know that the zone weakens by every revisits, so looking at how price behaves around the zones is smethig very important too.\n\nHope that makes sence, Best, Mel","a":"@mel","d":"","n":"#215","p":9,"im":["4ee54bdabb1119b6d67c74eb4951bfb0fc62dbab","7eb40ad778ee827c92c1ebd3d00e108ae88c64aa"],"m":215},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_216","t":"I am now considering these assignments as graduate school assignments. I will post and complete based on the schedule I have given myself.\n\nAnywork thus far is not considered agfaqinst the assignment\n\nHomework Recieved 8/15/2012 from IF\n\nSet up a subfolder for CP Homework and get into the charts Complete Find at least 20 CP setups, at HTF S/D zones, and explain what you see on each chart\n\nAlso chart the bigger picture where the CP occurred\n\nWhile you're looking for CP, take the time to find at least 20 CPLQ (Liquidity) too\n\nIf you're not used to these, you can get stopped out of some fantastic trades and deeply regret not knowing why.","a":"Nosbigs","d":"","n":"#216","p":9,"im":[],"m":216},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_217","t":"I am new to Supply and Demand trading method. My first attempt of CP homework..\n\nPlease comment..","a":"pipextract","d":"","n":"#217","p":9,"im":["1935f0bd353ea65ff8b0d76415a4ac9309dc8b9e"],"m":217},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_218","t":"Hi everyone,\n\nContinuing to watch the live market for eye training and to record down the factors that seem to lead into each homework setup.","a":"Simon","d":"","n":"#218","p":9,"im":["3110504575453deb01e4b04d12492a4d89c62d97"],"m":218},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_219","t":"Keep it up Simon, you've got a good eye for this","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#219","p":9,"im":[],"m":219},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_220","t":"Nice work, but don't ignore untested zones within what looks like a continuous CP","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#220","p":9,"im":["2d9fe41026cd31ec824ccee6a6649ae2fb223f78"],"m":220},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_221","t":"Hi Dr. Pipextract\n\nAbout your EU Compression, if you look at bigger TF, you will see the opposite story. In Weekly EU is approaching compressed to Demand, allowing the buyers get on top.\n\nIts just a thumb rule to remember that the HTF has the greater effect.\n\nSo this to explain the failing of the Daily CP you have spotted.","a":"benhur","d":"","n":"#221","p":9,"im":["0366e5df757f417e3c435d362173a1c62a1b9075"],"m":221},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_222","t":"Another way to answer your question -","a":"Ifmyante","d":"","n":"#222","p":9,"im":["514726ca0d1ef7b500a27891357907a01adac46e"],"m":222},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_223","t":"Hi Mel and Ifmyante\n\nThank you for taking the time to reply and critique my CP finds.\n\n@Mel Didn't make it to supply pic - Ah yes ill try and keep that in mind when drawing zones in future. Also your drawn supply zone was tested thrice which relates to your next reply for the loss pic.\n\nLoss pic - I guess such setups become a probability play? If you look at my first pic, the supply zone was tested multiple times and each test made a higher low just like how in the loss pic, each test made a lower high buy eventually led to a breakdown of the demand zone whereas in the first pic it was profitable.\n\nIfmyante I cant seem to see your attachment. I see a Attachment 17-09-201215-25-06.jpg not found error.","a":"nagato","d":"","n":"#223","p":9,"im":[],"m":223},{"id":"aboutcompression_p9_224","t":"CHART 21:\n\nCHART 22:\n\nCHART 23:\n\nCHART 24:\n\nCHART 25:\n\nCHART 26:\n\nCHART 27:\n\nCHART 28:\n\nCHART 29:\n\nCHART 30:\n\nCHART 31 - INDEX:\n\nCHART 32:\n\nCHART 33:\n\nCHART 34:\n\nCHART 36:\n\nCHART 37 - INDEX:\n\nCHART 38:\n\nCHART 39:\n\nCHART 40:\n\nCHART 41:\n\nCHART 42 - INDEX:\n\nCHART 43:\n\nCHART 44:","a":"Bushido","d":"","n":"#224","p":9,"im":["cb132e871dd2609e0d06192f38c6b97ca12dbd70","32123c90e1654044163256d220d2dc905a62f2e5","79e9c6ff4e0e121bce4